From dcf5c0ad2c2a0986558070dfeeff2cca122cae30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:25:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] perf(text): stop creating a GL texture for each texture
 drawable frame

TextureSpecialDrawable created a ResourceTexture, bound it and "closed" it
every frame. Binding generates a new, empty GL texture; AbstractTexture's
close() is a no-op, so the texture name was never deleted. The quad is
drawn through RenderLayer.getText(identifier), whose texture phase binds
the real texture from the TextureManager (loading it on first use) when
the batch is drawn, so the temporary texture never affected the output.
Remove it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TD7PJ5R7t7hM3ymeeqXP4H
---
 .../mishang/uc/text/TextureSpecialDrawable.java | 17 +++++++----------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main/java/pers/solid/mishang/uc/text/TextureSpecialDrawable.java b/src/main/java/pers/solid/mishang/uc/text/TextureSpecialDrawable.java
index 72698318..ac4d9838 100644
